{
  "status": "Adopted in ordinary and default native compilers; remaining excessive memory unresolved.",
  "patch": "--- a/comp.ts\n+++ b/comp.ts\n@@ -678,6 +678,7 @@\n }\n \n function memo_gc(): void {\n+  PROBES.length = 1; // Keep DUMMY; opened binders belong to this definition.\n   [OPENS, USES, FOLDS, SPINES, CONSTS, TELES, TAILS, LAYS].forEach((m) => m.clear());\n }\n \n",
  "scope_audit": [
    "memo_gc is called only at reachable-definition discovery, native top-level definition compilation, and JavaScript top-level definition compilation. Nested native calls do not clear it.",
    "OPENS contains opened bodies/probes; USES contains numeric probe indices. Both clear at the same boundary.",
    "Def.h is raised from closed checked syntax. def_raise opens it for inspection without storing the opened body in the definition.",
    "SIGS retains declared parameter types plus immutable layouts, not opened runtime binder probes. NODES retains layouts only.",
    "emit_open resets the per-function uses map; persistent emitted segments retain strings, references by name, and layouts.",
    "DUMMY is the one persistent probe, kept at index zero."
  ],
